WEBVTT

00:00:03.003 --> 00:00:06.530
Captain's Log,
Stardate 53556.4.

00:00:06.606 --> 00:00:08.574
We've towed
a damaged vessel aboard

00:00:08.641 --> 00:00:09.869
and are attempting to repair it

00:00:09.943 --> 00:00:12.207
while the Doctor treats
the Qomarian crew

00:00:12.278 --> 00:00:14.610
who have suffered
minor injuries.

00:00:15.682 --> 00:00:16.774
Stay away.

00:00:16.850 --> 00:00:18.943
If you don't cooperate,
I can't treat you.

00:00:19.019 --> 00:00:20.509
When we agreed
to be examined

00:00:20.587 --> 00:00:22.179
by this ship's
Medical Officer,

00:00:22.255 --> 00:00:23.722
we didn't know that you were

00:00:23.790 --> 00:00:25.280
a primitive computer matrix.

00:00:25.358 --> 00:00:27.292
I assure you there is
nothing primitive about me.

00:00:27.360 --> 00:00:28.622
Hmm.

00:00:28.695 --> 00:00:29.753
I am programmed to perform

00:00:29.829 --> 00:00:31.626
more than five million
medical procedures.

00:00:31.698 --> 00:00:33.632
Does that include
bloodletting?

00:00:33.700 --> 00:00:36.828
No, but I'll be happy to
add it to my repertoire.

00:00:38.471 --> 00:00:44.341
We are ready to
return to our ship.

00:00:44.411 --> 00:00:48.643
Could you contact one
of your superiors?

00:00:48.715 --> 00:00:49.943
Doctor to the Captain.

00:00:50.016 --> 00:00:51.415
Please report to Sick Bay.

00:00:51.484 --> 00:00:52.974
Already on my way.

00:00:53.053 --> 00:00:57.547
The Captain is
coming here now.

00:00:57.624 --> 00:01:04.792
If you want to talk to her,
you can have a seat.

00:01:08.501 --> 00:01:11.937
It is a very
irritating program.

00:01:12.005 --> 00:01:15.805
Maybe we can disable
its speech subroutines.

00:01:18.511 --> 00:01:20.604
You're not authorized
to do that.

00:01:20.680 --> 00:01:21.977
How are our guests?

00:01:23.016 --> 00:01:24.313
Their injuries are minor.

00:01:24.384 --> 00:01:26.318
Unfortunately, I
can't say the same

00:01:26.386 --> 00:01:27.785
for their lack of manners.

00:01:27.854 --> 00:01:28.786
Doctor.

00:01:28.855 --> 00:01:30.823
What is the status
of our ship?

00:01:30.890 --> 00:01:31.948
To be honest,

00:01:32.058 --> 00:01:33.650
we're having a little trouble

00:01:33.726 --> 00:01:35.694
understanding your technology.

00:01:35.762 --> 00:01:37.730
The problem is your technology.

00:01:37.797 --> 00:01:40.891
Interference from your
antiquated scanning devices

00:01:40.967 --> 00:01:43.128
shut down
our propulsion system.

00:01:43.203 --> 00:01:45.068
Forgive us, Captain.

00:01:45.138 --> 00:01:46.969
We live
in a closed system.

00:01:47.107 --> 00:01:48.665
We are not accustomed

00:01:48.741 --> 00:01:51.141
to interacting
with other species,

00:01:51.211 --> 00:01:53.076
especially inferior ones.

00:01:53.146 --> 00:01:55.080
Well, then...

00:01:55.148 --> 00:01:59.983
I guess we'll leave the repairs
in your superior hands.

00:02:00.086 --> 00:02:02.418
Our injuries will have
to be treated first.

00:02:02.489 --> 00:02:04.719
Is there someone other
than this hologram

00:02:04.791 --> 00:02:05.758
who could help us?

00:02:05.825 --> 00:02:08.259
No one who's better qualified.

00:02:08.328 --> 00:02:10.262
Hmm.

00:02:10.330 --> 00:02:11.592
Very well.

00:02:11.664 --> 00:02:13.097
Try to bear with our

00:02:13.166 --> 00:02:16.431
deficiencies
just a little longer.

00:02:20.006 --> 00:02:21.473
This way, please.

00:02:37.657 --> 00:02:41.616
I've been working
on the railroad

00:02:41.694 --> 00:02:45.425
All the livelong day

00:02:45.498 --> 00:02:47.625
I've been working
on the railroad

00:02:47.700 --> 00:02:50.965
Just to pass the time away...

00:02:51.037 --> 00:02:53.403
What is that?

00:02:53.473 --> 00:02:54.735
This?

00:02:54.807 --> 00:02:56.297
A hypospray.

00:02:56.376 --> 00:02:57.308
No.

00:02:57.377 --> 00:02:58.969
What you were doing.

00:02:59.112 --> 00:03:00.807
Preparing your medication.

00:03:00.880 --> 00:03:01.812
No.

00:03:01.881 --> 00:03:03.405
With your voice.

00:03:05.151 --> 00:03:07.449
You mean... singing?

00:03:07.520 --> 00:03:09.920
"Singing."

00:03:09.989 --> 00:03:11.422
Do it again.

00:03:11.491 --> 00:03:13.959
Yes, do it again.

00:05:06.639 --> 00:05:09.506
Someone's in the kitchen
with Dinah

00:05:09.575 --> 00:05:12.339
Someone's in the kitchen
I know-ow-ow-ow

00:05:12.412 --> 00:05:15.313
Someone's in the kitchen
with Dinah

00:05:15.381 --> 00:05:18.248
Strummin' on the old banjo
and singin'

00:05:18.318 --> 00:05:21.082
Fee, fi, fiddle-ee-i-o

00:05:21.154 --> 00:05:24.021
Fee, fi,
fiddle-ee-i-o-o-o-o

00:05:24.090 --> 00:05:29.187
Fee, fi, fiddle-ee-i-o...

00:05:29.262 --> 00:05:32.095
Strummin' on the old banjo.

00:05:32.165 --> 00:05:35.601
It is a unique
mathematical variation.

00:05:35.668 --> 00:05:36.862
Difficult to quantify.

00:05:36.936 --> 00:05:39.700
How do you suppose
the algorithms are generated?

00:05:39.772 --> 00:05:40.932
Maybe it's a fractal.

00:05:41.040 --> 00:05:42.701
Or wave-form calculus.

00:05:42.775 --> 00:05:45.801
Do you mean to say a culture
as superior as yours

00:05:45.878 --> 00:05:49.143
has never heard music
of any kind?

00:05:49.215 --> 00:05:50.944
There are other
kinds of music?

00:05:51.017 --> 00:05:52.450
Of course.

00:05:52.518 --> 00:05:55.954
The little ditty I just sang is
an early American folk song,

00:05:56.022 --> 00:05:58.081
but countless cultures
have produced

00:05:58.157 --> 00:05:59.556
thousands of types of...

00:05:59.625 --> 00:06:00.887
music...

00:06:00.960 --> 00:06:04.225
instrumental,
choral, orchestral.

00:06:04.297 --> 00:06:05.491
What is the purpose

00:06:05.565 --> 00:06:07.157
of this "music"?

00:06:07.233 --> 00:06:10.498
Is it an encryption
code of some kind?

00:06:10.570 --> 00:06:13.596
There is a mathematical
component to music,

00:06:13.673 --> 00:06:17.234
but primarily it's a form
of artistic expression.

00:06:17.310 --> 00:06:20.245
"Artistic expression"?

00:06:20.313 --> 00:06:22.247
Using sounds and images

00:06:22.315 --> 00:06:25.250
to convey ideas and emotions.

00:06:25.318 --> 00:06:27.115
Why would anyone do that?

00:06:27.186 --> 00:06:31.919
Well... to... communicate
their feelings.

00:06:31.991 --> 00:06:35.188
Can't they do that
through speech?

00:06:35.261 --> 00:06:38.059
Yes, but music
is much more...

00:06:38.131 --> 00:06:40.759
expressive and entertaining.

00:06:40.833 --> 00:06:42.266
You mean to say

00:06:42.335 --> 00:06:45.793
that this "music" is...
recreational?

00:06:48.508 --> 00:06:50.237
It does have
other applications.

00:06:50.309 --> 00:06:52.869
Uh, as a matter of fact,
I've recently been doing

00:06:52.945 --> 00:06:56.938
some research into
its therapeutic properties,

00:06:57.016 --> 00:06:58.813
but... yes, primarily,

00:06:58.885 --> 00:07:02.480
we use it for... enjoyment.

00:07:03.956 --> 00:07:05.014
"We"?

00:07:05.091 --> 00:07:07.321
You mean to say
others aboard your ship

00:07:07.393 --> 00:07:09.884
are capable
of producing this phenomenon?

00:07:09.962 --> 00:07:12.328
Well, maybe not
with my level of expertise,

00:07:12.398 --> 00:07:14.992
but there are
quite a few members of this crew

00:07:15.067 --> 00:07:16.557
who possess musical skills.

00:07:16.636 --> 00:07:19.070
Maybe we judged this
culture too quickly.

00:07:19.138 --> 00:07:20.571
Hmm.

00:07:20.640 --> 00:07:22.073
Our database contains
the works

00:07:22.141 --> 00:07:24.075
of thousands
of musicians and composers.

00:07:24.143 --> 00:07:26.907
If you'd like, I could download
some selections for you.

00:07:26.979 --> 00:07:30.437
Could you sing them for us?

00:07:34.086 --> 00:07:35.917
Captain's Log, supplemental.

00:07:36.055 --> 00:07:39.252
The Qomar have
completed repairs to their ship

00:07:39.325 --> 00:07:40.485
and, surprisingly,

00:07:40.560 --> 00:07:43.154
have invited us
to visit their system.

00:07:43.229 --> 00:07:46.494
Apparently, it's no longer
"closed" to outsiders.

00:07:47.567 --> 00:07:49.933
Harry, can you make sense
of any of this?

00:07:50.002 --> 00:07:52.596
We're picking up thousands
of subspace transmissions,

00:07:52.672 --> 00:07:53.934
all encrypted differently.

00:07:54.073 --> 00:07:56.473
Between the satellites
and the spacecraft,

00:07:56.542 --> 00:07:58.942
it's like navigating
an obstacle course.

00:07:59.011 --> 00:08:00.103
With all this traffic,

00:08:00.179 --> 00:08:01.874
the Qomar might not
even know we're here.

00:08:01.948 --> 00:08:02.880
Apparently, they do.

00:08:02.949 --> 00:08:04.280
We are being hailed.

00:08:04.350 --> 00:08:07.046
Captain, you now have

00:08:07.119 --> 00:08:10.384
the privilege
of meeting Prelate Koru.

00:08:10.456 --> 00:08:13.448
Welcome to the Qomar
Planetary Alliance.

00:08:13.526 --> 00:08:14.652
Thank you, Prelate.

00:08:14.727 --> 00:08:15.887
We're looking forward

00:08:16.028 --> 00:08:17.586
to learning more
about your culture.

00:08:17.663 --> 00:08:20.029
Our civilization is
no doubt intimidating.

00:08:20.099 --> 00:08:21.361
We'll do what we can

00:08:21.434 --> 00:08:23.732
to avoid overwhelming
you during your stay.

00:08:23.803 --> 00:08:24.997
I appreciate that.

00:08:25.071 --> 00:08:28.905
I understand
we're not as advanced as you,

00:08:29.008 --> 00:08:31.101
but we're fast learners,
and we'd like to...

00:08:31.177 --> 00:08:32.109
We want to learn more

00:08:32.178 --> 00:08:34.772
about the algorithmic
expressions

00:08:34.847 --> 00:08:36.246
you call "music."

00:08:36.315 --> 00:08:38.215
We're prepared
to give you complete access

00:08:38.284 --> 00:08:40.013
to our musical database,
as well as...

00:08:40.086 --> 00:08:41.576
Your Emergency Medical Hologram.

00:08:41.654 --> 00:08:44.122
We'd consider an
exchange of technology

00:08:44.190 --> 00:08:47.159
if you give us complete
access to this device.

00:08:47.226 --> 00:08:49.717
I believe he's made
some recordings.

00:08:49.795 --> 00:08:51.888
No, not recordings.

00:08:55.334 --> 00:08:56.926
How about a recital?

00:08:57.036 --> 00:08:59.596
"Recital"?

00:08:59.672 --> 00:09:01.162
A live performance.

00:09:01.240 --> 00:09:02.502
We can put
together a program

00:09:02.575 --> 00:09:03.769
of various styles of music.

00:09:03.843 --> 00:09:06.835
Uh, will the Emergency
Medical Hologram sing?

00:09:06.913 --> 00:09:09.609
He'll be the star attraction.

00:09:45.284 --> 00:09:46.546
Thank you.

00:09:46.619 --> 00:09:48.109
You're very kind.

00:09:49.689 --> 00:09:51.156
That was a selection

00:09:51.223 --> 00:09:54.192
from the opera Don Carlos,
composed by Giuseppe Verdi,

00:09:54.260 --> 00:09:56.820
a towering figure
in Earth's musical history.

00:10:02.034 --> 00:10:04.594
Another human musical form
is called "jazz,"

00:10:04.670 --> 00:10:07.696
which has flourished
since the early 20th century.

00:10:07.773 --> 00:10:10.173
Mathematically, you'll find
the rhythmic structures

00:10:10.242 --> 00:10:13.803
quite interesting, particularly
the use of syncopation

00:10:13.879 --> 00:10:16.347
which is said
to make the music swing.

00:10:17.984 --> 00:10:19.884
You may also notice
some fascinating

00:10:19.952 --> 00:10:22.477
trigonometric functions
in the counterpoint,

00:10:22.555 --> 00:10:25.683
but I suppose I'm going off
on a tangent, aren't I?

00:10:28.961 --> 00:10:30.724
He's very funny.

00:10:30.796 --> 00:10:32.286
So, without further ado,

00:10:32.365 --> 00:10:34.765
I give you Harry Kim
and the Kimtones.

00:11:03.663 --> 00:11:07.155
We wish to hear the Doctor.

00:11:07.233 --> 00:11:08.393
Yes, the Doctor.

00:11:08.467 --> 00:11:09.866
Bring back the Doctor.

00:11:09.935 --> 00:11:11.402
We want the Doctor to sing.

00:11:11.470 --> 00:11:13.700
Doc, they're dying up there.

00:11:13.773 --> 00:11:15.968
You've got to do something.

00:11:17.343 --> 00:11:19.675
Pick up the tempo.

00:11:21.681 --> 00:11:25.947
That old black magic has me
in its spell

00:11:26.018 --> 00:11:30.045
That old black magic
that you weave so well

00:11:30.122 --> 00:11:34.616
Those icy fingers
up and down my spine

00:11:34.694 --> 00:11:39.290
The same old witchcraft
when your eyes meet mine

00:11:39.365 --> 00:11:43.301
The same old tingle
that I feel inside

00:11:43.369 --> 00:11:47.635
And then,
that elevator starts its ride

00:11:47.707 --> 00:11:49.971
And down and down I go

00:11:50.042 --> 00:11:52.806
'Round and 'round I go

00:11:52.878 --> 00:11:55.676
Like a leaf
that's caught in the tide...

00:11:58.384 --> 00:11:59.476
Well, if you like jazz,

00:11:59.552 --> 00:12:00.814
you're going to love
rock 'n' roll.

00:12:00.886 --> 00:12:03.150
It was one of the 20th century's
greatest inventions.

00:12:03.222 --> 00:12:06.055
Does the Doctor sing
rock 'n' roll?

00:12:06.125 --> 00:12:07.922
I wouldn't say it's
his favorite genre.

00:12:08.027 --> 00:12:10.928
No, he's more
of an opera man.

00:12:11.030 --> 00:12:14.090
As am I.

00:12:17.002 --> 00:12:18.799
Aren't you one
of the musicians?

00:12:20.272 --> 00:12:21.261
Harry Kim.

00:12:21.340 --> 00:12:22.272
Vinka.

00:12:22.341 --> 00:12:23.899
Welcome aboard Voyager.

00:12:23.976 --> 00:12:26.604
Um, if you'd like to see
the rest of the ship,

00:12:26.679 --> 00:12:28.169
I'd be happy to
give you a tour.

00:12:28.247 --> 00:12:29.441
Maybe later.

00:12:29.515 --> 00:12:32.006
I was wondering if you could
introduce me to the Doctor.

00:12:33.853 --> 00:12:36.117
Congratulations, Doctor,
you stole the show.

00:12:36.188 --> 00:12:39.385
Thank you, Captain,
but I can't take all the credit.

00:12:39.458 --> 00:12:42.655
There was something in the air,
a certain magic.

00:12:42.728 --> 00:12:44.161
It was one of those
rare moments

00:12:44.230 --> 00:12:48.360
when audience and performer
become one.

00:12:48.434 --> 00:12:49.526
Doctor.

00:12:49.602 --> 00:12:50.534
Prelate.

00:12:50.603 --> 00:12:52.230
Tincoo.

00:12:52.304 --> 00:12:55.467
I will introduce your singing
to more of our people.

00:12:55.541 --> 00:12:57.441
I'm flattered.

00:12:57.510 --> 00:12:58.807
You will perform on our planet.

00:12:58.878 --> 00:12:59.936
I'd consider it an honor,

00:13:00.012 --> 00:13:01.775
but you'll have to negotiate
the terms

00:13:01.847 --> 00:13:03.337
with my... representative.

00:13:04.550 --> 00:13:06.484
I don't understand.

00:13:06.552 --> 00:13:09.077
I believe the Doctor
is referring to me, Prelate.

00:13:09.155 --> 00:13:11.555
Another concert would mean
extending our stay.

00:13:11.624 --> 00:13:14.115
When would you want
to schedule the performance?

00:13:14.193 --> 00:13:16.058
As soon as possible.

00:13:16.128 --> 00:13:17.425
The Doctor could perform

00:13:17.496 --> 00:13:19.293
at one of the lecture halls
at the university.

00:13:19.365 --> 00:13:21.162
I'm not sure a lecture hall

00:13:21.233 --> 00:13:23.667
would meet
the acoustic requirements.

00:13:23.736 --> 00:13:25.431
I'll help you make

00:13:25.504 --> 00:13:28.268
whatever modifications
you think are necessary.

00:13:28.340 --> 00:13:31.537
Sounds like you've got yourself
a booking, Doctor.

00:13:33.212 --> 00:13:35.680
I'd like to reproduce a backdrop

00:13:35.748 --> 00:13:38.239
which was used in
a production of Pagliacci

00:13:38.317 --> 00:13:39.909
at Teatro de la Scala...

00:13:39.985 --> 00:13:41.953
Earth's most famous
opera house.

00:13:42.021 --> 00:13:43.215
It's beautiful.

00:13:43.289 --> 00:13:45.314
Your taste in design
is as refined

00:13:45.391 --> 00:13:46.824
as your taste in music.

00:13:46.892 --> 00:13:48.189
We'll replicate it for you.

00:13:48.260 --> 00:13:49.659
Excellent,

00:13:49.728 --> 00:13:52.720
but we still have the problem
with the sight lines.

00:13:52.798 --> 00:13:55.323
What's wrong
with the sight lines?

00:13:55.401 --> 00:13:57.392
If you consider the height
of the average Qomar,

00:13:57.469 --> 00:13:59.801
it's obvious that anyone
seated in the back five rows

00:13:59.872 --> 00:14:01.533
will have an obstructed view.

00:14:01.607 --> 00:14:02.574
You're right.

00:14:02.641 --> 00:14:04.268
They won't be able
to see anything

00:14:04.343 --> 00:14:05.571
but the top of your head.

00:14:05.644 --> 00:14:07.009
The glare could blind them.

00:14:09.148 --> 00:14:11.708
You'll have to excuse
Lieutenant Torres.

00:14:11.784 --> 00:14:14.082
Her appreciation
of music is limited

00:14:14.153 --> 00:14:16.883
to a smattering
of Klingon drinking songs.

00:14:16.956 --> 00:14:18.218
We'll have to increase

00:14:18.290 --> 00:14:20.781
the rake of the floor
by five degrees.

00:14:20.860 --> 00:14:22.487
You really think
they're going to redesign

00:14:22.561 --> 00:14:24.495
an entire building just
to appeal to your vanity?

00:14:24.563 --> 00:14:27.191
Vanity has nothing
to do with it, Lieutenant.

00:14:27.266 --> 00:14:29.257
I'm concerned
about my audience.

00:14:29.335 --> 00:14:31.803
We are prepared to make
whatever changes

00:14:31.871 --> 00:14:34.237
the Doctor thinks
are necessary.

00:14:34.306 --> 00:14:36.240
Thank you, Tincoo.

00:14:36.308 --> 00:14:37.468
While we're at
it, Lieutenant,

00:14:37.543 --> 00:14:39.204
I'll need some help
with my wardrobe.

00:14:39.278 --> 00:14:41.576
I'm an Engineer,
not a costume designer.

00:14:41.647 --> 00:14:43.410
I'd like you to make
an adjustment

00:14:43.482 --> 00:14:45.575
to my mobile emitter
that would allow me

00:14:45.651 --> 00:14:47.448
to make quick changes
between songs.

00:14:47.519 --> 00:14:48.577
That sounds exciting.

00:14:48.654 --> 00:14:49.848
Oh, it will be.

00:14:49.922 --> 00:14:53.915
I plan to segue from
Don Juan to Rigoletto

00:14:53.993 --> 00:14:55.324
in the blink of an eye.

00:14:55.394 --> 00:14:56.918
It will be a triumph of...

00:14:56.996 --> 00:14:58.759
Arrogance
and self-absorption?

00:15:00.733 --> 00:15:02.997
Just trying to help.

00:15:06.238 --> 00:15:09.332
Your crewmates don't seem
to appreciate your abilities.

00:15:09.408 --> 00:15:11.000
You've noticed that, too.

00:15:11.076 --> 00:15:14.045
That must be very
frustrating for you.

00:15:14.113 --> 00:15:16.411
You have no idea.

00:15:20.986 --> 00:15:23.477
We'll be starting
in two minutes.

00:15:23.555 --> 00:15:25.819
I'd better get into costume.

00:15:28.294 --> 00:15:29.454
How do I look?

00:15:29.528 --> 00:15:32.759
You look perfect.

00:15:40.139 --> 00:15:43.165
I wish I had a subroutine
to eliminate preshow jitters.

00:15:43.242 --> 00:15:45.335
I could help you
add one to your program.

00:15:45.411 --> 00:15:47.777
You're very sweet.

00:15:47.846 --> 00:15:49.473
I'm just a little... nervous.

00:15:49.548 --> 00:15:50.742
Why?

00:15:50.816 --> 00:15:53.683
I'm about to expose your
entire culture to music

00:15:53.752 --> 00:15:54.878
for the first time.

00:15:54.954 --> 00:15:56.945
The responsibility
is... enormous.

00:15:57.056 --> 00:15:59.547
Your performance tonight
will be transmitted

00:15:59.625 --> 00:16:01.718
to hundreds of millions
of people.

00:16:01.794 --> 00:16:04.456
Is that supposed
to help me relax?

00:16:07.933 --> 00:16:09.400
It's time.

00:16:54.079 --> 00:16:55.376
Report.

00:16:55.447 --> 00:16:57.074
I didn't order a
Red Alert, Captain.

00:16:57.149 --> 00:16:58.844
Well, someone did.

00:16:58.917 --> 00:17:01.044
The command
originated in...

00:17:01.120 --> 00:17:03.145
Astrometrics.

00:17:03.222 --> 00:17:04.849
Seven of Nine to the Captain.

00:17:04.923 --> 00:17:07.255
I've found evidence
that the Qomar are attempting

00:17:07.326 --> 00:17:09.419
to sabotage Voyager.

00:17:09.495 --> 00:17:11.725
On my way.

00:17:14.299 --> 00:17:16.324
What have you got?

00:17:16.402 --> 00:17:17.892
I believe the Qomar
are attempting

00:17:18.003 --> 00:17:19.698
to disable our com system.

00:17:19.772 --> 00:17:20.739
How?

00:17:20.806 --> 00:17:22.205
By overloading it
with millions

00:17:22.274 --> 00:17:23.639
of teraquads of
irrelevant data.

00:17:23.709 --> 00:17:25.609
What do you mean
by "irrelevant"?

00:17:31.116 --> 00:17:34.176
They're transmissions...

00:17:34.253 --> 00:17:36.346
all addressed to the Doctor.

00:17:36.422 --> 00:17:37.912
Precisely.

00:17:37.990 --> 00:17:40.481
I've only been able
to decipher

00:17:40.559 --> 00:17:42.186
a small fraction
of them so far,

00:17:42.261 --> 00:17:43.489
but they include invitations

00:17:43.562 --> 00:17:45.393
to social
and scientific functions,

00:17:45.464 --> 00:17:47.523
requests
for personal encounters,

00:17:47.599 --> 00:17:50.932
and cloying tributes
to the Doctor's talents.

00:17:51.036 --> 00:17:53.266
Computer, stand down Red Alert.

00:17:53.338 --> 00:17:55.397
This isn't sabotage, Seven.

00:17:55.474 --> 00:17:57.772
This is fan mail.

00:17:57.843 --> 00:17:59.538
Fan mail?

00:17:59.611 --> 00:18:01.078
People who admire
performers

00:18:01.146 --> 00:18:02.773
are called "fans."

00:18:02.848 --> 00:18:05.476
The word, I believe,
derives from "fanatic."

00:18:05.551 --> 00:18:06.984
Exactly.

00:18:07.052 --> 00:18:10.419
Why would the Doctor inspire
fanaticism among the Qomar?

00:18:10.489 --> 00:18:12.286
Music is new to them.

00:18:12.357 --> 00:18:14.848
Clearly, they're
very excited about it.

00:18:14.927 --> 00:18:16.121
This glorification

00:18:16.195 --> 00:18:18.390
of the individual
is irrational.

00:18:18.464 --> 00:18:21.433
The Doctor is merely reproducing
the work of others.

00:18:21.500 --> 00:18:23.900
Why do his fans fixate
solely on him?

00:18:24.036 --> 00:18:26.630
I suppose he's the embodiment
of what they admire.

00:18:26.705 --> 00:18:28.900
He can do something
they can't,

00:18:28.974 --> 00:18:30.498
and that makes
him special.

00:18:30.576 --> 00:18:32.908
Perhaps, but that doesn't
explain their interest

00:18:32.978 --> 00:18:34.639
in the minutiae
of the Doctor's life.

00:18:34.713 --> 00:18:36.112
"What does he do

00:18:36.181 --> 00:18:37.739
in his spare time?"

00:18:37.816 --> 00:18:39.681
"To how many decimal places

00:18:39.751 --> 00:18:42.276
can he calculate pi?"

00:18:42.354 --> 00:18:46.085
This one wants to know his
favorite quadratic equation.

00:18:46.158 --> 00:18:47.853
People have
always fantasized

00:18:47.926 --> 00:18:50.451
about knowing
celebrities personally.

00:18:50.529 --> 00:18:53.930
I suppose it's a way of making
themselves feel more important.

00:18:54.032 --> 00:18:55.590
Tuvok to Janeway.

00:18:55.667 --> 00:18:57.100
Go ahead.

00:18:57.169 --> 00:18:59.569
We have a security problem
on Deck 2.

00:18:59.638 --> 00:19:00.935
On my way.

00:19:02.608 --> 00:19:04.235
Just think, Seven.

00:19:04.309 --> 00:19:06.800
As personal friends
of the Doctor,

00:19:06.879 --> 00:19:09.712
we're the envy of
millions of Qomar.

00:19:14.052 --> 00:19:15.644
Our efforts to
accommodate them

00:19:15.721 --> 00:19:17.382
have gotten out of hand.

00:19:17.456 --> 00:19:19.481
I guess their interest
in the Doctor

00:19:19.558 --> 00:19:21.150
is greater
than we expected.

00:19:23.028 --> 00:19:24.461
Much greater.

00:19:24.530 --> 00:19:26.725
I recommend we refuse
all further requests

00:19:26.798 --> 00:19:28.265
for transport
from the surface.

00:19:28.333 --> 00:19:29.630
Agreed.

00:19:29.701 --> 00:19:30.633
And we should evacuate

00:19:30.702 --> 00:19:31.862
these visitors immediately.

00:19:31.937 --> 00:19:34.030
They are interfering with
normal ship's functions.

00:19:34.106 --> 00:19:36.472
Tuvok, when have functions
aboard this ship

00:19:36.542 --> 00:19:37.668
ever been normal?

00:20:11.210 --> 00:20:12.837
Thank you for coming.

00:20:12.911 --> 00:20:14.572
Please accept this eight
by ten by four

00:20:14.646 --> 00:20:15.840
singing replica of me.

00:20:15.914 --> 00:20:17.040
Thank you so...

00:20:17.115 --> 00:20:19.549
One at a time,
one at a time, now.

00:20:19.618 --> 00:20:23.076
Please, now, do not touch
the Doctor's mobile emitter.

00:20:23.155 --> 00:20:24.850
Captain.

00:20:24.923 --> 00:20:26.322
Isn't this exciting?

00:20:26.391 --> 00:20:28.951
I'm not sure that's
the word I'd use for it.

00:20:29.027 --> 00:20:29.959
Excuse me.

00:20:30.095 --> 00:20:31.585
Sorry, excuse me.

00:20:31.663 --> 00:20:32.960
I'm sorry, Captain,

00:20:33.098 --> 00:20:34.622
but you'll have
to wait your turn

00:20:34.700 --> 00:20:35.792
like everybody else.

00:20:35.867 --> 00:20:37.425
I'm not here
for an autograph.

00:20:37.502 --> 00:20:38.696
We need to talk.

00:20:42.608 --> 00:20:44.803
I'm glad you're enjoying
yourself, Doctor,

00:20:44.876 --> 00:20:46.673
but this is getting
a little excessive.

00:20:46.745 --> 00:20:48.804
I'm only doing what
I can to ensure

00:20:48.880 --> 00:20:51.974
that first contact with
the Qomar goes smoothly.

00:20:52.084 --> 00:20:54.382
Does that include
using our replicator reserves

00:20:54.453 --> 00:20:56.819
to create miniaturized
versions of yourself?

00:20:56.888 --> 00:20:58.446
I would never
do such a thing.

00:20:58.523 --> 00:21:00.821
As a matter of fact,
the Qomar have devoted

00:21:00.892 --> 00:21:02.257
an entire holo
processing plant

00:21:02.327 --> 00:21:03.726
to manufacturing
them for me.

00:21:03.795 --> 00:21:05.387
I see.

00:21:05.464 --> 00:21:08.228
Well, in any case, you've been
neglecting your Sick Bay duties.

00:21:08.300 --> 00:21:10.325
I haven't received
a report in three days.

00:21:10.402 --> 00:21:12.063
Oh, come now, Kathryn.

00:21:12.137 --> 00:21:13.604
It's not as though

00:21:13.672 --> 00:21:16.402
there's been a flood
of medical emergencies.

00:21:16.475 --> 00:21:19.569
I wasn't aware we were
on a first name basis.

00:21:19.645 --> 00:21:21.135
I-I meant "Captain."

00:21:21.213 --> 00:21:22.475
I'm sorry.

00:21:22.547 --> 00:21:24.447
Oh, that's perfectly
all right, Doctor,

00:21:24.516 --> 00:21:25.949
or do you prefer "Maestro"?

00:21:26.051 --> 00:21:27.780
Please.

00:21:27.853 --> 00:21:29.150
Either is acceptable.

00:21:29.221 --> 00:21:32.315
Well, then, let me make
it clear to both of you:

00:21:32.391 --> 00:21:35.155
Maestro, you're finished
for today.

00:21:35.227 --> 00:21:38.355
Doctor, report
to Sick Bay, now.

00:21:46.305 --> 00:21:47.670
Well, well, well.

00:21:47.739 --> 00:21:50.799
If it isn't
the wandering minstrel.

00:21:50.876 --> 00:21:53.367
What's the nature of their
medical emergencies?

00:21:53.445 --> 00:21:55.538
Apparently,
these two young ladies

00:21:55.614 --> 00:21:57.411
became dizzy and disoriented

00:21:57.482 --> 00:22:00.246
while waiting in line
to see you.

00:22:00.319 --> 00:22:02.014
I'll take over from here.

00:22:02.087 --> 00:22:03.315
Be careful, Doc.

00:22:03.388 --> 00:22:06.721
You seem to be hazardous
to the Qomars' health.

00:22:06.792 --> 00:22:07.884
I'm Vinka.

00:22:07.959 --> 00:22:09.392
I'm Azen.

00:22:09.461 --> 00:22:11.361
Hmm. Neither of you
appears to be ill.

00:22:11.430 --> 00:22:14.058
We wanted to meet you
in a more intimate setting.

00:22:14.132 --> 00:22:17.499
So we told your security
officer we were sick.

00:22:17.569 --> 00:22:19.161
Sick Bay is for medical
treatment only.

00:22:19.237 --> 00:22:20.670
I'm afraid you'll
have to leave.

00:22:20.739 --> 00:22:22.934
But there's so much
about you we want to know.

00:22:23.041 --> 00:22:24.736
Yes, you're a very
stimulating hologram.

00:22:24.810 --> 00:22:26.243
L-if you're here for a replica,

00:22:26.311 --> 00:22:27.744
they're available
in the Mess Hall.

00:22:27.813 --> 00:22:29.041
We don't want a replica.

00:22:29.114 --> 00:22:30.911
We want
the full-sized version.

00:22:30.982 --> 00:22:32.813
I-I-I'm flattered,
really, but if you

00:22:32.884 --> 00:22:34.749
don't leave now,
I'll have to call Security.

00:22:34.820 --> 00:22:37.948
I'll bet you can calculate pi
to over a thousand digits.

00:22:38.056 --> 00:22:39.546
Security to Sick Bay.

00:22:39.624 --> 00:22:42.593
Have you ever balanced
simultaneous equations?

00:22:42.661 --> 00:22:45.596
Computer, deactivate
Emergency Medical Hologram.

00:22:55.974 --> 00:22:57.965
Here you are.

00:22:58.043 --> 00:23:00.409
I needed to find
some peace and quiet.

00:23:00.479 --> 00:23:02.447
I want to show
you something.

00:23:04.015 --> 00:23:05.175
What's this?

00:23:05.250 --> 00:23:06.512
You inspired me to create

00:23:06.585 --> 00:23:08.678
my own musical composition.

00:23:08.754 --> 00:23:12.155
It's based on the intersection
of two fractals.

00:23:12.224 --> 00:23:14.419
Tincoo, this is extraordinary.

00:23:14.493 --> 00:23:16.120
I created it for you.

00:23:18.130 --> 00:23:19.927
I don't know what to say.

00:23:19.998 --> 00:23:21.488
Will you sing it?

00:23:21.566 --> 00:23:23.431
I'm not sure I can.

00:23:23.502 --> 00:23:25.936
It's very complex.

00:23:33.378 --> 00:23:34.470
The melody's lovely,

00:23:34.546 --> 00:23:36.173
but some
of these notes are well beyond

00:23:36.248 --> 00:23:37.510
the human vocal range.

00:23:37.582 --> 00:23:38.947
You are not human.

00:23:39.084 --> 00:23:40.847
No, but...

00:23:40.919 --> 00:23:42.716
I can help you reconfigure
your vocal processors.

00:23:42.788 --> 00:23:44.119
I don't think there's time.

00:23:44.189 --> 00:23:45.656
My last concert's tomorrow.

00:23:45.724 --> 00:23:48.659
Why does it have to be
your last concert?

00:23:48.727 --> 00:23:50.592
Because Voyager is scheduled
to depart.

00:23:50.662 --> 00:23:52.254
Stay here with us.

00:23:52.330 --> 00:23:54.560
I have responsibilities
on Voyager.

00:23:54.633 --> 00:23:56.100
They're a resourceful crew.

00:23:56.168 --> 00:23:58.068
I am certain they
will find a way

00:23:58.136 --> 00:24:00.570
to compensate
for your absence.

00:24:00.639 --> 00:24:03.130
I'm not so sure about that...

00:24:03.208 --> 00:24:06.905
but even if they could...

00:24:06.978 --> 00:24:09.879
Voyager's the only
life I've ever known.

00:24:09.948 --> 00:24:11.381
The crew are my friends.

00:24:11.450 --> 00:24:14.749
But they don't appreciate you
the way we do... you know that.

00:24:14.820 --> 00:24:18.847
You could have a new
life here as a performer,

00:24:18.924 --> 00:24:21.916
surrounded by people
who admire and respect

00:24:22.027 --> 00:24:23.324
your talent.

00:24:23.395 --> 00:24:25.192
It's very tempting, but...

00:24:25.263 --> 00:24:29.393
By any mathematical standard,
the medical care of 150 people

00:24:29.468 --> 00:24:33.871
cannot compare to the cultural
enrichment of millions.

00:24:33.939 --> 00:24:38.103
You can't always explain things
with an equation, Tincoo.

00:24:38.176 --> 00:24:41.407
What about the simplest equation
of them all?

00:24:41.480 --> 00:24:44.074
One plus one.

00:24:44.149 --> 00:24:47.050
I don't understand.

00:24:47.118 --> 00:24:49.814
The time you have been here

00:24:49.888 --> 00:24:53.585
has been the most stimulating
of my life.

00:24:56.928 --> 00:24:59.556
I feel the same way
about my time with you.

00:24:59.631 --> 00:25:01.360
Then stay here...

00:25:01.433 --> 00:25:03.298
with me.

00:25:13.211 --> 00:25:15.509
You're resigning
your commission?

00:25:15.580 --> 00:25:18.378
I've been asked to stay.

00:25:20.919 --> 00:25:22.181
When this all started,

00:25:22.254 --> 00:25:25.849
I thought you might have
a little harmless fun,

00:25:25.924 --> 00:25:27.915
and that
you'd be responsible enough

00:25:27.993 --> 00:25:29.460
to keep it in perspective.

00:25:29.528 --> 00:25:31.462
I can see now
that I was mistaken.

00:25:31.530 --> 00:25:34.465
This isn't "harmless fun"
for me, Captain.

00:25:34.533 --> 00:25:38.560
It's a once-in-a-lifetime
opportunity to realize a dream.

00:25:38.637 --> 00:25:40.468
What about your duty to Voyager?

00:25:40.539 --> 00:25:42.734
I take that
very seriously, but...

00:25:42.807 --> 00:25:44.035
You're a part of this ship.

00:25:44.109 --> 00:25:46.441
You sound as if you're talking
about a piece of equipment.

00:25:46.511 --> 00:25:47.535
That's not what I meant.

00:25:47.612 --> 00:25:48.704
Then shouldn't I be given

00:25:48.780 --> 00:25:49.940
the same respect

00:25:50.081 --> 00:25:51.878
as any flesh and blood
member of this crew?

00:25:51.950 --> 00:25:53.474
Every member of this crew

00:25:53.552 --> 00:25:55.918
is expected to fulfill
his obligations.

00:25:55.987 --> 00:25:58.956
If Harry Kim met an alien woman
on an away mission,

00:25:59.024 --> 00:26:00.457
fell in love and decided

00:26:00.525 --> 00:26:02.755
to spend the rest
of his life with her,

00:26:02.827 --> 00:26:05.990
raise a family, instead
of continuing on this journey,

00:26:06.064 --> 00:26:07.895
you wouldn't stand in his way.

00:26:07.966 --> 00:26:09.593
You're not Harry Kim.

00:26:09.668 --> 00:26:12.569
You're an Emergency
Medical Hologram.

00:26:12.637 --> 00:26:15.128
Then you do see me
as a piece of technology.

00:26:15.206 --> 00:26:18.039
I have given you
extraordinary freedom...

00:26:18.109 --> 00:26:23.069
to explore your creativity,
to go on away missions,

00:26:23.148 --> 00:26:25.343
to pursue personal
relationships...

00:26:25.417 --> 00:26:26.543
but enough is enough.

00:26:26.618 --> 00:26:27.607
Why?!

00:26:27.686 --> 00:26:28.778
Because you don't see me

00:26:28.853 --> 00:26:30.252
as an equal,
and you never have.

00:26:30.322 --> 00:26:31.311
Admit it.

00:26:31.389 --> 00:26:32.515
I am responsible

00:26:32.591 --> 00:26:34.252
for the medical needs
of this crew.

00:26:34.326 --> 00:26:37.022
If I let you leave,
what kind of Captain would I be?

00:26:37.095 --> 00:26:39.928
Every other Starfleet officer
chose to be here,

00:26:40.031 --> 00:26:42.295
but I never had a choice...
until now.

00:26:42.367 --> 00:26:45.268
I've given this crew everything
for five years.

00:26:45.337 --> 00:26:46.634
Isn't it worth anything?

00:26:46.705 --> 00:26:48.138
Haven't I earned the right

00:26:48.206 --> 00:26:50.800
to self-determination?

00:26:53.612 --> 00:26:55.910
You've lost other systems before

00:26:55.981 --> 00:26:58.677
and always managed
to find a solution.

00:26:58.750 --> 00:27:00.581
You'll manage without me.

00:27:00.652 --> 00:27:01.846
What about you?

00:27:01.920 --> 00:27:04.150
Will you manage without us?

00:27:04.222 --> 00:27:06.383
The Qomar are a technologically
advanced species.

00:27:06.458 --> 00:27:08.551
I have no doubt that
my maintenance requirements

00:27:08.627 --> 00:27:09.753
will be met.

00:27:09.828 --> 00:27:10.886
Now which one of us

00:27:10.996 --> 00:27:13.191
is looking at you as
a piece of technology?

00:27:13.264 --> 00:27:15.664
I'm not talking about
your maintenance needs.

00:27:15.734 --> 00:27:17.827
I'm talking about
your emotional needs.

00:27:17.902 --> 00:27:20.598
You've got people on this
ship who care about you.

00:27:20.672 --> 00:27:23.436
The Qomar certainly seem
to care about me.

00:27:23.508 --> 00:27:25.908
And when their tastes change?

00:27:25.977 --> 00:27:28.070
What makes you think
that's going to happen?

00:27:28.146 --> 00:27:30.341
Fame is often temporary.

00:27:30.415 --> 00:27:32.349
This isn't just about fame.

00:27:32.417 --> 00:27:34.612
Oh, really?

00:27:34.686 --> 00:27:36.916
If you must know...

00:27:36.988 --> 00:27:39.252
there's a woman involved,

00:27:39.324 --> 00:27:46.321
one who appreciates me in a way
no one on this crew ever has.

00:27:52.937 --> 00:27:56.236
Well, it sounds like
you'll have everything you need.

00:27:59.277 --> 00:28:00.209
I believe I will.

00:28:00.278 --> 00:28:01.245
I hope so, Doctor,

00:28:01.312 --> 00:28:02.870
because once Voyager's gone,

00:28:02.947 --> 00:28:05.882
you won't be able
to change your mind.

00:28:06.017 --> 00:28:08.815
That's a risk
I'm willing to take.

00:28:08.887 --> 00:28:10.616
As your Captain,

00:28:10.689 --> 00:28:14.216
I should refuse
this resignation,

00:28:14.292 --> 00:28:16.886
but as your friend,

00:28:16.961 --> 00:28:19.759
it wouldn't be right
to stand in your way.

00:28:29.674 --> 00:28:32.006
And you can't let the
Captain ignore her health.

00:28:32.077 --> 00:28:33.908
She's notorious for
finding any excuse

00:28:34.045 --> 00:28:35.307
to miss her appointments.

00:28:35.380 --> 00:28:36.904
I'll send her
weekly reminders.

00:28:36.981 --> 00:28:38.642
And when Mr. Neelix
becomes convinced

00:28:38.717 --> 00:28:40.742
that he's suffering
from the Toluncan Ague...

00:28:40.819 --> 00:28:42.252
which he does
every flu season...

00:28:42.320 --> 00:28:44.447
don't argue with him,
just give him a placebo.

00:28:44.522 --> 00:28:47.457
Doc, I've been assisting
you for three years.

00:28:47.525 --> 00:28:48.583
I know the drill.

00:28:48.660 --> 00:28:51.185
Yes, I suppose you do.

00:28:51.262 --> 00:28:52.752
Remember, I'll be
within com range

00:28:52.831 --> 00:28:53.923
for at least another month,

00:28:53.998 --> 00:28:55.522
so if any problems
should arise...

00:28:55.600 --> 00:28:56.726
Doc...

00:28:56.801 --> 00:28:59.929
you're not really going
to do this, are you?

00:29:00.038 --> 00:29:02.563
I would have thought
you of all people

00:29:02.640 --> 00:29:04.471
would be glad to see me go.

00:29:04.542 --> 00:29:05.668
Are you kidding?

00:29:05.744 --> 00:29:08.679
Who am I going to torment
after you're gone?

00:29:12.283 --> 00:29:14.217
Well...

00:29:14.285 --> 00:29:16.185
I've got some more good-byes.

00:29:16.254 --> 00:29:18.882
I'll check in with you
before I leave.

00:29:20.959 --> 00:29:23.553
I'll be here...

00:29:23.628 --> 00:29:25.858
redecorating your office.

00:29:38.309 --> 00:29:40.903
Hello, Seven.

00:29:40.979 --> 00:29:46.246
I wanted to see
you before I left.

00:29:46.317 --> 00:29:48.615
I've downloaded
some social lessons

00:29:48.686 --> 00:29:50.153
we haven't covered yet.

00:29:50.221 --> 00:29:51.916
There are 17 new chapters.

00:29:51.990 --> 00:29:53.924
Does one of them
include instructions

00:29:54.025 --> 00:29:55.287
for ending a friendship?

00:29:56.427 --> 00:29:58.520
Our friendship's
not over, Seven.

00:29:58.596 --> 00:30:00.359
It will be difficult to maintain

00:30:00.431 --> 00:30:02.228
if we never see
each other again.

00:30:04.936 --> 00:30:06.927
I know it'll be hard
for you when I'm gone.

00:30:07.071 --> 00:30:08.368
I will adapt.

00:30:10.608 --> 00:30:13.600
Yes, I suppose you will,

00:30:13.678 --> 00:30:16.875
but it'll be hard for me.

00:30:16.948 --> 00:30:18.210
Why?

00:30:18.283 --> 00:30:20.843
You're getting everything
you've ever wanted.

00:30:20.919 --> 00:30:22.887
I thought you'd
be the first one

00:30:22.954 --> 00:30:26.583
to understand my desire
to grow as an individual.

00:30:26.658 --> 00:30:28.421
What I don't understand

00:30:28.493 --> 00:30:31.553
is why you can't do that
aboard Voyager.

00:30:31.629 --> 00:30:34.393
I feel I've accomplished
all I can here.

00:30:34.465 --> 00:30:36.831
Oh, there's the occasional
medical mystery

00:30:36.901 --> 00:30:38.766
that challenges
my programming,

00:30:38.837 --> 00:30:40.828
but mostly it's
become routine

00:30:40.905 --> 00:30:42.930
and frankly, I
feel my talents

00:30:43.007 --> 00:30:44.941
are often taken for granted.

00:30:45.009 --> 00:30:48.410
But when I'm standing
on that stage performing,

00:30:48.479 --> 00:30:51.880
and I see those rapt
faces in the audience...

00:30:54.252 --> 00:30:56.584
I feel I finally
know what it's like

00:30:56.654 --> 00:30:58.588
to be made of
flesh and blood.

00:30:58.656 --> 00:31:01.250
You simply crave attention,
applause,

00:31:01.326 --> 00:31:02.623
fan mail.

00:31:04.295 --> 00:31:05.557
What if I do?

00:31:05.630 --> 00:31:07.257
Those things
are irrelevant.

00:31:07.332 --> 00:31:09.095
To you, maybe,

00:31:09.167 --> 00:31:14.571
but to me, it makes me
feel appreciated,

00:31:14.639 --> 00:31:17.437
even loved...

00:31:17.508 --> 00:31:21.035
Not for what
I've been programmed to do,

00:31:21.112 --> 00:31:23.273
but for who I've become.

00:31:23.348 --> 00:31:26.909
Doctor, you're receiving
a transmission.

00:31:26.985 --> 00:31:28.919
Route it to Cargo Bay 2.

00:31:28.987 --> 00:31:30.352
Doctor, this is Tincoo.

00:31:30.421 --> 00:31:32.321
I want to see you immediately.

00:31:32.390 --> 00:31:34.255
I have something to show you.

00:31:34.325 --> 00:31:35.451
What is it?

00:31:35.526 --> 00:31:36.652
A surprise.

00:31:36.728 --> 00:31:38.593
I think you'll be very pleased.

00:31:38.663 --> 00:31:40.631
I'll beam down
as soon as I can.

00:31:42.333 --> 00:31:43.322
Seven...

00:31:43.401 --> 00:31:45.631
You shouldn't keep
your fans waiting.

00:32:14.966 --> 00:32:16.263
Thank you

00:32:16.334 --> 00:32:17.824
for being so prompt.

00:32:17.902 --> 00:32:19.733
Of course.

00:32:19.804 --> 00:32:21.829
What's the surprise?

00:32:21.906 --> 00:32:23.339
I had an inspiration.

00:32:23.408 --> 00:32:25.376
Another musical composition?

00:32:25.443 --> 00:32:26.603
Better.

00:32:31.416 --> 00:32:32.576
What's this?

00:32:32.650 --> 00:32:34.811
I've solved
all our problems.

00:32:36.988 --> 00:32:38.819
I wasn't aware
that we had any.

00:32:38.890 --> 00:32:41.222
Well, you were reluctant
to leave your ship,

00:32:41.292 --> 00:32:43.055
and you also doubted
your ability

00:32:43.127 --> 00:32:45.721
to sing my composition,
so I created a superior

00:32:45.797 --> 00:32:47.526
holo-matrix.

00:32:47.598 --> 00:32:49.930
I-I don't understand.

00:32:50.001 --> 00:32:52.196
It's simple.

00:32:52.270 --> 00:32:56.866
Now you can stay aboard Voyager,
and he can sing for us.

00:32:56.941 --> 00:32:58.238
Listen.

00:33:20.798 --> 00:33:23.096
You can't make
a superior singer

00:33:23.167 --> 00:33:25.260
simply by creating
a new matrix.

00:33:25.336 --> 00:33:27.133
I beg to differ.

00:33:27.205 --> 00:33:29.105
My vocal processors
are enhanced

00:33:29.173 --> 00:33:30.834
with polyphonic sequencers.

00:33:30.908 --> 00:33:32.375
I am not only capable

00:33:32.443 --> 00:33:34.434
of singing notes
well beyond your limited range,

00:33:34.512 --> 00:33:36.912
I can produce
multiharmonic overtones

00:33:36.981 --> 00:33:39.575
through the use
of amplitude vacillat...

00:33:41.753 --> 00:33:43.846
Why did you do that?

00:33:43.921 --> 00:33:45.946
Tincoo, music is more
than mathematics,

00:33:46.057 --> 00:33:47.388
and I am much more

00:33:47.458 --> 00:33:50.484
than a program
with musical subroutines.

00:33:52.363 --> 00:33:55.298
All of my experience,
all of my passion

00:33:55.366 --> 00:33:58.130
goes into every note
that I sing.

00:33:58.202 --> 00:34:01.433
When you listen to me,
when my singing moves you,

00:34:01.506 --> 00:34:04.270
you're not just hearing notes.

00:34:04.342 --> 00:34:06.310
You're hearing my artistry...

00:34:06.377 --> 00:34:08.504
my... soul.

00:34:08.579 --> 00:34:10.911
I've duplicated that, too.

00:34:11.015 --> 00:34:13.711
I thought you wanted me.

00:34:13.785 --> 00:34:16.583
I did,
but now, I've developed

00:34:16.654 --> 00:34:20.522
a far more sophisticated
piece of technology.

00:34:20.591 --> 00:34:23.856
Technology...

00:34:23.928 --> 00:34:26.260
I thought you would be pleased.

00:34:26.330 --> 00:34:28.821
You seemed reluctant
to leave your ship.

00:34:28.900 --> 00:34:31.733
You told me that the time
you had spent with me

00:34:31.803 --> 00:34:34.795
was the most stimulating
of your life.

00:34:34.872 --> 00:34:36.305
It was.

00:34:36.374 --> 00:34:39.172
You inspired me
to do my greatest work.

00:34:39.243 --> 00:34:40.369
But I thought...

00:34:42.547 --> 00:34:43.946
Yes?

00:34:44.082 --> 00:34:46.312
That you and I...

00:34:48.686 --> 00:34:50.779
What?

00:34:56.427 --> 00:35:00.727
Well, I suppose I'm no longer
on the bill tomorrow.

00:35:00.798 --> 00:35:02.197
Of course you are.

00:35:02.266 --> 00:35:05.235
It will be
your farewell performance.

00:35:07.171 --> 00:35:10.163
Of course.

00:35:20.384 --> 00:35:21.851
You wanted to see me?

00:35:21.919 --> 00:35:25.377
I need your clearance code
to delete my medical database.

00:35:25.456 --> 00:35:27.754
You sure you want
to do that?

00:35:27.825 --> 00:35:29.588
If you give one of your fans
a heart attack,

00:35:29.660 --> 00:35:30.820
you won't be able

00:35:30.895 --> 00:35:32.294
to resuscitate him.

00:35:32.363 --> 00:35:34.661
I need more space
in my matrix.

00:35:34.732 --> 00:35:35.790
For what?

00:35:35.867 --> 00:35:38.358
To expand
my musical subroutines,

00:35:38.436 --> 00:35:41.894
so that I can sing
this composition.

00:35:41.973 --> 00:35:44.669
Well, I'm surprised
you're asking me for help.

00:35:44.742 --> 00:35:47.768
I recall your saying that
my appreciation for music

00:35:47.845 --> 00:35:51.872
was limited to "a smattering
of Klingon drinking songs."

00:35:51.949 --> 00:35:53.849
Please, B'Elanna.

00:35:53.918 --> 00:35:55.681
I'm asking you as a friend.

00:35:55.753 --> 00:35:58.722
Everything depends on this.

00:35:58.789 --> 00:36:01.553
What's so important
about this composition?

00:36:01.626 --> 00:36:03.218
Tincoo wrote it for me.

00:36:03.294 --> 00:36:04.556
Your girlfriend?

00:36:04.629 --> 00:36:07.257
I wouldn't call her that.

00:36:07.331 --> 00:36:09.322
Don't tell me you
two had a fight.

00:36:09.400 --> 00:36:10.890
Let's just say,

00:36:10.968 --> 00:36:14.734
she doesn't appreciate me quite
as much as I thought she did.

00:36:14.805 --> 00:36:16.067
But that will all change.

00:36:16.140 --> 00:36:17.232
Once I perform this,

00:36:17.308 --> 00:36:18.900
she will see me for
the artist I truly am.

00:36:18.976 --> 00:36:22.844
Look, Doc, I don't know
anything about this woman,

00:36:22.914 --> 00:36:24.905
or why she doesn't
appreciate you,

00:36:24.982 --> 00:36:27.212
and I may not be
an expert on music,

00:36:27.285 --> 00:36:29.651
but I'm
a pretty good Engineer.

00:36:29.720 --> 00:36:32.314
I can expand your musical
subroutines all you like.

00:36:32.390 --> 00:36:34.688
I can even reprogram you
to be a whistling teapot,

00:36:34.759 --> 00:36:39.196
but, if I do that,
you won't be you anymore.

00:36:49.640 --> 00:36:51.699
Tonight, I was planning
to perform a song

00:36:51.776 --> 00:36:53.573
composed by one
of your own people.

00:36:53.644 --> 00:36:56.841
When you consider she heard
music for the first time

00:36:56.914 --> 00:36:58.108
only a few days ago,

00:36:58.182 --> 00:37:01.174
it's an extraordinary
accomplishment.

00:37:01.252 --> 00:37:03.880
But although it's
a very beautiful composition,

00:37:04.021 --> 00:37:08.583
I'm afraid
it's beyond my abilities.

00:37:13.664 --> 00:37:19.125
So instead, I'm going to sing
an old Neapolitan ballad.

00:37:19.203 --> 00:37:22.001
It's a song about lost love.

00:39:01.339 --> 00:39:02.431
Thank you, Doctor.

00:39:02.506 --> 00:39:03.598
That was fascinating.

00:39:03.674 --> 00:39:05.039
It is because

00:39:05.109 --> 00:39:09.239
of your inspiration
that I can now present to you

00:39:09.313 --> 00:39:13.773
a new and exciting
musical program... a singing

00:39:13.851 --> 00:39:15.148
holographic matrix...

00:39:16.620 --> 00:39:20.283
designed specifically
to extend the range

00:39:20.358 --> 00:39:23.225
of humanoid vocal capabilities,

00:39:23.294 --> 00:39:27.594
singing
my own musical composition.

00:40:24.021 --> 00:40:25.318
Come in.

00:40:29.026 --> 00:40:30.960
Good morning, Captain.

00:40:31.028 --> 00:40:32.996
What's this?

00:40:34.498 --> 00:40:36.295
A formal request

00:40:36.367 --> 00:40:37.664
to be reinstated.

00:40:39.703 --> 00:40:43.537
So you've taken off your tails
and put them between your legs.

00:40:45.209 --> 00:40:46.676
Yes, ma'am.

00:40:46.744 --> 00:40:49.907
You offended a lot of people
who care about you.

00:40:49.980 --> 00:40:51.242
I know.

00:40:51.315 --> 00:40:52.839
I was a fool, I'm sorry,

00:40:52.917 --> 00:40:56.375
and I'm willing to do whatever
I can to rectify the situation,

00:40:56.454 --> 00:40:59.855
starting with the deletion
of all my musical subroutines.

00:40:59.924 --> 00:41:01.323
Permission denied.

00:41:01.392 --> 00:41:02.188
But, Captain...

00:41:02.259 --> 00:41:03.317
No "buts," Doctor.

00:41:03.394 --> 00:41:05.021
You're expected
to follow orders,

00:41:05.095 --> 00:41:07.063
just like every other
flesh and blood

00:41:07.131 --> 00:41:08.758
member of this crew.

00:41:08.833 --> 00:41:11.927
Resume your normal activities...

00:41:12.002 --> 00:41:13.492
all of them.

00:41:13.571 --> 00:41:15.664
Yes, ma'am.

00:41:15.739 --> 00:41:17.366
Dismissed.

00:41:35.292 --> 00:41:37.522
Oh, Seven, I didn't see you.

00:41:37.595 --> 00:41:38.755
I suppose

00:41:38.829 --> 00:41:40.729
you've come to gloat.

00:41:40.798 --> 00:41:42.732
I have something for you.

00:41:42.800 --> 00:41:43.960
What is it?

00:41:44.034 --> 00:41:45.626
Fan mail.

00:41:45.703 --> 00:41:47.568
Delete it.

00:41:47.638 --> 00:41:49.833
I don't want
to read another word.

00:41:49.907 --> 00:41:51.568
Then I'll read it for you.

00:41:51.642 --> 00:41:52.904
Seven...

00:41:52.977 --> 00:41:54.569
"Dear Doctor,

00:41:54.645 --> 00:41:56.977
"I regret that your
last performance

00:41:57.114 --> 00:41:59.674
"was not as successful
as you'd hoped.

00:41:59.750 --> 00:42:02.218
"There are still
those who appreciate

00:42:02.286 --> 00:42:05.915
"your unique talents
and admire you as an individual.

00:42:05.990 --> 00:42:10.290
I'll always consider myself
your loyal fan."

00:42:10.361 --> 00:42:12.420
Who's it from?

00:42:14.465 --> 00:42:16.797
It's signed, "Seven of Nine

00:42:16.867 --> 00:42:19.927
Tertiary Adjunct
of Unimatrix 01."

00:42:45.362 --> 00:42:48.889
I've been working
on the railroad

00:42:48.966 --> 00:42:52.561
All the livelong day

00:42:52.636 --> 00:42:55.969
I've been working
on the railroad

00:42:56.040 --> 00:43:00.238
Just to pass the time away

00:43:00.311 --> 00:43:04.247
Can't you hear
the whistle blowing?

00:43:04.315 --> 00:43:07.807
Rise up
so early in the morn...
